    "description": "Hudson Transmission owns and operates a transmission interconnector linking New Jersey and Manhattan. Its customer base is the regional power market, with capacity contracted to support transfers between PJM and New York City load zones. The project operates a contracted transmission model rather than a traditional rate-regulated utility model. Public materials describe a 660-megawatt underground and underwater link that entered service in 2013 and includes associated transmission upgrades in New Jersey. The asset is strategically positioned to move power into New York City and has historically supported a long-term arrangement with the New York Power Authority. Argo signed to acquire Hudson Transmission in 2018 and public materials describe principal equity ownership as acquired in early 2019 through a managed investment vehicle. Current ownership percentages are not publicly disclosed.",
